        <detaileddescription>
<para>Rows [0, r) of the upper triangle of the Gram matrix of the m vectors rows[0 .. m): out[i * m + j] = &lt;rows[i], rows[j]&gt; for i &lt; r and i &lt; j &lt; m. The Gram matrix of m vectors is the m x m matrix of their inner products. In a local join of <ref refid="structfaiss_1_1DeterministicNNDescent" kindref="compound">DeterministicNNDescent</ref>, the first r vectors are the new members, so these are the pairs with at least one new member. The vectors are read in place. The kernel also sets some entries with j &lt;= i. The sums have a fixed order, so the values do not depend on the thread. Defined for AVX2, AVX512 and ARM_NEON. The dispatch uses AVX512 on the higher AVX-512 levels and ARM_NEON on ARM_SVE, and the caller uses BLAS for the other levels. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
